# Kin: more of the same, the small change of living together (Docs/Design/30-towns-and-talk.md). Elders and the young
# who aren't kin, friends in foul weather, quarrels over small things that are never small.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Old and young, not kin

scene kn_mix_elder_pup_street
when topic=smalltalk a.stage=old b.stage=young band=acquaintances|strangers
a : Mind where you're running, pup! | Whose pup are you? | Don't throw stones at the hens.
b : Sorry! | The tanner's. | They threw them first.
a : Sorry doesn't mend old bones. | I know your mother. Behave. | Hens don't throw stones.
b : I'll run slower. | Everyone knows her. | These ones do.
a : Run somewhere else. | That's why. | Go on with you.

scene kn_mix_teen_elder_respect
when topic=smalltalk a.stage=adolescent b.stage=old band=acquaintances|strangers
a : Can I carry that for you? | Do you need a paw with that door? | Is it true you remember the old king?
b : I'm not dead yet. But yes. | It sticks. Push it with your shoulder. | I remember his funeral. Long, dull, rainy.
a : There. Where to? | There. | Was he a good king?
b : Home. Slowly. I'll tell you stories. | Good pup. | He was a king. That's all they ever are.
a : Long ones? | Any time. | That's not an answer.
b : The longest. | Good. | It's the only true one.

scene kn_mix_old_strangers
when topic=smalltalk a.stage=old b.stage=old band=strangers|acquaintances
a : Cold for the season. | The young have no respect anymore. | My knees say rain.
b : It was colder in my day. | They never did. We didn't either. | Mine say storm.
a : Everything was, in our day. | Speak for yourself. I was a delight. | Yours are more honest.
b : Colder and better. | I'm sure. | Older, anyway.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Friends in foul weather

scene kn_fr_storm_shelter
when topic=friends weather=storm|rain
a : Come in out of that, you'll drown. | You look like a drowned rat. | Shake off outside, please!
b : Thank you. It's the end of days out there. | Thank you. That's how I feel. | Too late. Sorry.
a : Sit by the fire. | Here. A blanket. | You've soaked the whole doorway.
b : You're a good friend. | It smells of dog. | I'll mop it.
a : I know. | It is dog. Lie on it. | With what?

scene kn_fr_snow_day
when topic=friends weather=snow
a : Snow's too deep to work. | Fancy a walk in it? | The pups are out pelting the watch with snowballs.
b : Best news all week. | Only if you break the trail. | Bright One bless them.
a : Then we've the whole day. | I always break the trail. | The watch is throwing back.
b : Then we waste it properly. | You always break it crooked. | Then it's war.
a : At the tavern. | It's scenic. | And I know which side I'm on.

scene kn_fr_fog
when topic=friends weather=fog
a : I nearly walked into the well. | I could barely see my own tail this morning. | Is that you? I thought you were a cart.
b : Follow your nose, not your eyes. | Then smell your way. | Do I look like a cart?
a : My nose found the baker's instead. | It found the midden. | In this fog, everyone does.
b : Better than the well. | Worse than the well. | Charming.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Small quarrels

scene kn_q_late_again
when topic=quarrel|friends
a : You're late. Again. | I waited an hour at the well. | You said dawn. It's noon.
b : I'm here now. | Something came up. | Dawn's a feeling.
a : An hour after now. | Something always does. | Noon is a fact.
b : The best things are worth waiting for. | It won't next time. | Fine. I'm sorry.
a : You're not one of them. | It will. | Fine.

scene kn_q_borrowed_broken
when topic=quarrel
a : You broke my cart. | You gave back my axe with a nick in it. | My cloak's torn. You borrowed it.
b : It was old. | It was blunt anyway. | It was torn when you gave it me.
a : It was working. | It was sharp when I lent it! | It was whole!
b : It was working old. | Sharp-ish. | Whole-ish.
a : Fix it or pay. | Sharpen it, then. | Mend it.

scene kn_q_loud_neighbour
when topic=quarrel
a : Your pups woke the whole street. | Do you have to sing at midnight? | The hammering. Every morning. Before dawn.
b : They're pups. Pups make noise. | I sing when I'm happy. | I work before dawn.
a : Not that much noise. | Be happy quieter. | Then work quieter.
b : Teach me how and I will. | Happiness is loud. | Hammers aren't quiet.
a : Stuff a sock in them. | So's my temper. | Neither am I.

scene kn_q_cheated_bones
when topic=quarrel place=tavern
a : You cheated. I saw your paw. | Those bones are weighted. | That's the third six in a row.
b : I don't cheat. | They're my lucky bones. | I'm lucky tonight.
a : You cheated last week. | Lucky with lead in them. | Nobody's that lucky.
b : I won last week. | Weigh them yourself. | I am. Pay up.
a : We're done playing. | I will. | Never.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Family, the seasons

scene kn_fam_spring_clean
when topic=family band=family|spouses season=spring place=home
a : Spring cleaning. Everything out. | We're shedding everywhere. Get the brush. | Air the bedding. It smells of winter.
b : Everything? Even the cat? | Brush yourself. | Winter smells like home.
a : The cat first. | I can't reach my back. | Winter smells like old wolf.
b : She'll never forgive us. | Fine. Turn round. | ...Fine. Air it.
a : She never forgives us anyway. | Harder. Ah. There. | Thank you.

scene kn_fam_summer_harvest_kids
when topic=family band=family season=summer|autumn a.stage=adult b.stage=young|adolescent
a : Everyone helps with the harvest. Even you. | Carry the water to the field. | Stop eating the berries before they reach the basket.
b : My paws are too small. | It's so heavy. | I'm checking they're good.
a : Small paws pick small things. Go. | Half a bucket, then. | Are they?
b : Fine. | Half's still heavy. | Very good. I should check more.
a : Good pup. | Then make two trips. | Basket.

scene kn_fam_autumn_stores
when topic=family band=family|spouses season=autumn
a : We need more stored for winter. | The smokehouse is full. Good. | Did you salt the last of the meat?
b : We've as much as last year. | Full and stinking. | Most of it.
a : Last year we ran short. | Stinking means full. | Most isn't all.
b : Then a little more. | Full means winter. | Then I'll finish it.
a : A lot more. | Winter we can face. | Before it turns.

scene kn_fam_winter_hearth
when topic=family band=family season=winter time=dusk|night place=home
a : Everyone in close. Save the wood. | Tell the pups a story. | Whose turn is it to sleep by the door?
b : Close as cubs. | Which one? | Not mine.
a : That's how we survive. | The one about the winter wolf. | Everyone says that.
b : Warmest way. | They'll never sleep after. | Because it's true.
a : It is. | They never sleep anyway. | It's yours.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Friends, by work

scene kn_fr_workmates
when topic=friends|work
a : Same yard, same work, twenty years. | Remember your first day? You dropped everything. | Without you this job would kill me.
b : And still not rich. | I remember yours. You cried. | It's killing you anyway.
a : Rich in friends. | Only once. In the privy. | Slower, with you.
b : That doesn't buy bread. | Twice. | Same for me.
a : It buys cider. | Fine. Twice. | Good.

scene kn_fr_guard_merchant
when topic=friends a.role=guard b.role=merchant
a : Quiet day on your street? | Anyone giving you trouble? | Got any of those honey buns left?
b : Thanks to you. | Only the tax man. | For you, always.
a : I just stand here. | Can't arrest him, sadly. | You're a good friend.
b : Standing here is enough. | Pity. | Bring the watch by. Business is business.
a : I'll stand harder. | I'd like to. | I will.

scene kn_fr_healer_patient
when topic=friends a.job=healer
a : How's the leg? | Still taking the bitter tea? | You look better than last week.
b : Better. I can walk to the well. | Most days. | Thanks to you.
a : Then walk to the well and back. | Every day. | Thanks to the tea.
b : Slave driver. | It's foul. | And you.
a : Healer. | It works. | A little.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Acquaintances, by the hour

scene kn_acq_night_meeting
when topic=smalltalk band=acquaintances time=night
a : Late to be out. | Couldn't sleep either? | Going home?
b : I could say the same. | Never, these nights. | Eventually.
a : I'm on my way to bed. | Nor me. The moon's too bright. | Me too. Eventually.
b : So am I. Slowly. | Bright enough to read by. | Night, then.
a : Goodnight. | If I could read. | Goodnight.

scene kn_acq_dawn_meeting
when topic=smalltalk band=acquaintances time=dawn
a : Morning. | You're up with the birds. | Off somewhere?
b : Is it? Feels like night still. | Somebody has to be. | Work. Always work.
a : Morning by the bell. | The birds think so too. | Same.
b : The bell's a liar. | Birds don't work. | Then good luck to us both.

scene kn_acq_market_bump
when topic=smalltalk band=acquaintances place=market
a : Fancy meeting you here. | Buying for the household? | Have you seen the price of salt?
b : Everyone's here on market day. | Always. Never enough. | Don't. It hurts.
a : Even the ones you'd rather not see. | Never is. | It hurts my purse more.
b : Like the tax man. | Not with pups. | Mine's empty already.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Strangers, between sexes and ages

scene kn_str_young_old
when topic=smalltalk band=strangers a.stage=young|adolescent b.stage=adult|old
a : Are you a stranger? | Where are you from? | Why do you smell funny?
b : To you, I suppose. | Far from here. | It's called travelling. It doesn't wash off.
a : I've never seen you. | How far? | Does it come off ever?
b : Then I'm a stranger. | Far enough to be tired. | After a long bath.
a : My mother says don't talk to strangers. | I'm going to go far one day. | You should take one.

scene kn_str_courtesy
when topic=smalltalk band=strangers a.stage=adult b.stage=adult
a : After you. | Please, go ahead. | Excuse me. I'm in your way.
b : Thank you. | Thank you kindly. | Not at all.
a : Bright One's day to you. | Good day. | Good day to you.
